  "name": "HUMAN IMMUNODEFECIENCY VIRUS - 1 (HIV-1) QUALITATIVE PCR",
  "code": "2398",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>RESULT (IU/ML)</strong></th>\n<th><strong>REMARK</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Target Not Detected</strong></td>\n<td>Sample provided does not contain HIV RNA.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&lt;100</strong></td>\n<td>HIV RNA detected but below the lower limit of the linear range of the assay. These results should be interpreted with caution.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>100 - 1.0 &times; 10⁷</strong></td>\n<td>HIV RNA detected within the linear range of the assay.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&gt;1.0 &times; 10⁷</strong></td>\n<td>HIV RNA detected above the linear range of the assay.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>NOTE :</strong><br>An interpretation of \"Not Detected\" does not rule out the presence of PCR inhibitors in the patient specimen or HIV RNA<br>concentrations below the level of detection of the test.<br>Analytical Sensitivity : 100 IU/mL<br>Linear Range : 100 - 1.0 x 107</p>\n<p><br><strong>CLINICAL USE :</strong></p>\n<p><br>HIV-1 viral load is the primary marker of antiretroviral treatment effectiveness. Before treatment initiation, the viral load&nbsp;provides information on the risk of disease progression and establishes a baseline for assessing the effect of antiviral&nbsp;treatment. After treatment is initiated, a primary goal is to decrease the viral load below the limits of detection (LODs) of the&nbsp;available assays within 12 to 24 weeks. Thereafter, viral load measurement is useful in assessing the continuing&nbsp;effectiveness of therapy.</p>",
